# RedArt EDI — agent rules

## Product

Colorado Medicaid NEMT → X12 **837P** microservice for RedArt. Read `docs/HANDOFF.md` for full context.

## Coding conventions

- Apps live under `apps.*`; shared `BaseModel` in `apps.core`
- Approval-first for schema/API changes when the user’s rules require it; never invent migrations without ask unless they explicitly request migrate
- Serializers: validation only. Business helpers → `utils/service.py`; cleaning/parsers → `utils/validators.py`
- No N+1: use `select_related` / `prefetch_related` (see `NemtTrip.objects.with_relations()`)
- Soft delete by default; writes return `{id}` only; shared pagination `StandardPagination`
- Wire new APIs only in `redartdigital/api_v1_urls.py` (one `/api/v1/` include)
- Prefer human, minimal code — avoid AI-looking patterns (e.g. unnecessary `.only(*CONST)`)
- Do not over-index; unique constraints only when needed

## Domain locks

- TradingPartner ≠ ProviderBillingProfile
- Claim links via `trip_id` only (patient/provider through trip)
- Claim.status ≠ EDIFile.status
- ClaimDocument ≠ AttachmentSubmission
- Long-distance thresholds from `LongDistanceRule` DB, not hard-coded forever
- 837P EDI path separate from attachment channel

